    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a> united the feuding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sikhism">Sikh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#misl">Misls</a> into a single <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#punjab">Punjab</a> state, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lahore">Lahore</a> from 1799.</li><li>Its European-drilled army was among the strongest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#india">India</a>, and it governed a Muslim-majority population with a mixed-faith court.</li><li>Without institutions to manage succession, it collapsed into court intrigue after 1839 and was annexed by Britain in 1849.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> had the upper storeys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#golden-temple">Harmandir Sahib</a> covered in gilded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#copper">copper</a>, giving it its popular name: the Golden Temple.</p></aside>
    </section>

